{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790964652,"nonce":"MCh8ITn//0xf8wTpCFTzGZsuZIE=","title":"Several TieredRuntimes on parallel threads abort in osr::lazy_compile when calling functions by pointer","message":"With more than one TieredRuntime in one process, each on its own thread and each calling a function by its native pointer, the first-call compile aborts in osr::lazy_compile with \"a function compiled on first call could not be compiled\": the lazy compiler and its registry are process-wide, so one runtime's stub can resolve against another runtime's state. Calls by name are unaffected. Found by caribou while testing take_pending_error (08b2b443) and call_function (06c9b909); those by-pointer tests run one runtime per test process until this is fixed. Related: 2ce455c (a failed first-call compile aborts the process).","files":null}]}